    "text": {
     "en": "Digestion breaks big food pieces into small ones the body can absorb. It starts in the mouth where teeth chew and saliva acts on starch.\nFood goes through the food pipe to the stomach, where acids and juices work. The small intestine absorbs nutrients into the blood, and the large intestine removes water.\nUndigested waste leaves the body."
    }
